From 8b193e2f8b667541b6724e75d55124d95a2c6088 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AuraLite <auralite@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 15:56:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] NET N4: honest INTx (ledger D4)

The e1000 finally drives its interrupt line.  e1000_add seeds PCI cfg 0x3C
(Interrupt Line) = E1000_IRQ = 11 and 0x3D (Interrupt Pin) = INTA#, and
e1000_intx_update() drives pic_set_irq(m, 11, level) with the plan's
((ICR & IMS) != 0) condition -- on change only, the AHCI S5 pattern, with
the CHIPSET H7 fan-out to the I/O APIC inside pic_set_irq.  Every ICR/IMS
mutation recomputes the level: the TX walk, RX completion, ICS, ICR W1C,
IMS, IMC, ICR read-to-clear, and reset (CTRL.RST / device add).

N1 could not raise a line without an ack path; measured now, the ack path
is the PIC's INTA, the NIC payloads unmask IMS=0xD5 but run at IF=0 and
drain ICR before idling, and the PIC powers up with IMR=0xFF so a high pin
is not deliverable until a guest programs its masks.  The full handler
loop (intack -> vector 0x73 -> ICR drain -> pin drop -> EOI) is pinned by
test_net.c test_intx_line, including the guest's programming order (unmask
master IRQ2/cascade before the device raises, so the cascade edge latches).

Receipts: make test-unit green; n1/n2/n3 ALL PASS with byte-identical
receipts (the 76-frame N3 tape, N1TXOK ... icr=81, N3OK) and identical
wall time.  NC: revert src/e1000.c and test-net aborts at 'cfg 0x3C == 11'
(the "IRQ line 0" world).  No shipped receipt pinned that string.
